{"id": "wwdc2017-810", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2017/810", "wordCount": 1200, "segments": [{"start": 21.0, "text": "So what's new on iOS?"}, {"start": 25.0, "text": "For this release, a major theme"}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "has been Wayfinding."}, {"start": 29.0, "text": "Now Wayfinding traditionally"}, {"start": 30.0, "text": "refers to all the ways that we"}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "can help guide people through an"}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "environment and orient"}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "themselves within a physical"}, {"start": 37.0, "text": "space."}, {"start": 39.0, "text": "You encounter signage and"}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "information systems everywhere"}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "to help you find your way from"}, {"start": 45.0, "text": "street signs, to airports, and"}, {"start": 49.0, "text": "even in parking garages."}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "So naturally, our digital"}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "environments can benefit from"}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "clear navigation."}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "Wayfinding in UI can enhance"}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "your experience and"}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "understanding of the space that"}, {"start": 62.0, "text": "you're in."}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "Now when we design for iOS, our"}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "goal is to highlight content"}, {"start": 68.0, "text": "first."}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "But app layouts need clear"}, {"start": 71.0, "text": "visual hierarchy so that people"}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "know how to navigate through the"}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "system."}, {"start": 77.0, "text": "UI elements in general should"}, {"start": 79.0, "text": "not compete with content but"}, {"start": 81.0, "text": "help you to better understand"}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "potential functions and"}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "interactions."}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "And we are constantly trying to"}, {"start": 88.0, "text": "improve upon these themes."}, {"start": 89.0, "text": "So for iOS 11, we wanted to"}, {"start": 92.0, "text": "provide more clarity for"}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "navigation or Wayfinding"}, {"start": 95.0, "text": "throughout the system."}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "We wanted to focus on overall"}, {"start": 99.0, "text": "hierarchy through the use of"}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "typography."}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "And when it would be useful, we"}, {"start": 105.0, "text": "wanted to create greater"}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "contrast by refining elements"}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "within the UI."}, {"start": 110.0, "text": "So first, let's take a look at"}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "navigation."}, {"start": 115.0, "text": "Last year we started using more"}, {"start": 117.0, "text": "bold text in music because it's"}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "an app with a lot of dense"}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "content."}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "Text became instrumental for"}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "organizing similar media and"}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "orienting you while you browse"}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "and search."}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "And we recognize that other apps"}, {"start": 130.0, "text": "could benefit from the same text"}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "treatments."}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "So this year, we introduce large"}, {"start": 136.0, "text": "titles to navigation bars for"}, {"start": 138.0, "text": "other apps that could use some"}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "more emphasis."}, {"start": 142.0, "text": "This does not replace our"}, {"start": 143.0, "text": "standard navigation but is an"}, {"start": 145.0, "text": "opt-in version that transitions"}, {"start": 147.0, "text": "from to the standard Nav bar"}, {"start": 149.0, "text": "when you start scrolling."}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "Now you might be wondering where"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "these large titles should be"}, {"start": 156.0, "text": "used and I can highlight a"}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "couple guidelines to consider"}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "that we found helpful when"}, {"start": 161.0, "text": "deciding which of our apps"}, {"start": 163.0, "text": "they'd be most appropriate for."}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "A good place to use large-title"}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "navigation can be at the top"}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "level of an app with tabs."}, {"start": 170.0, "text": "This helps to understand that"}, {"start": 172.0, "text": "you're at a top level but also"}, {"start": 174.0, "text": "that you're scrolled to the top"}, {"start": 175.0, "text": "of the page."}, {"start": 177.0, "text": "Again, music is a good example"}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "of an app that uses large titles"}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "for all of its top levels but"}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "also occasionally on some"}, {"start": 186.0, "text": "secondary levels or further"}, {"start": 187.0, "text": "down."}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "Since music has so much content"}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "and multiple levels that you can"}, {"start": 192.0, "text": "drill into, large titles are"}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "helpful as you navigate further"}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "into the app."}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "They can be used for views that"}, {"start": 201.0, "text": "all have very similar layouts as"}, {"start": 204.0, "text": "a quick read on where you are."}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "Phone is an appropriate app to"}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "use large titles because almost"}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "all of the tabs show content in"}, {"start": 213.0, "text": "rows of text."}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "And it's important to stress"}, {"start": 217.0, "text": "that it's not always necessary"}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "to use large titles in"}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "navigation."}, {"start": 222.0, "text": "We found that in multiple"}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "scenarios it would hinder"}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "usability and not help."}, {"start": 227.0, "text": "And a good example of that is"}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "the clock app."}, {"start": 231.0, "text": "Even though it's an app with"}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "tabs, it doesn't have multiple"}, {"start": 236.0, "text": "content to sort through and each"}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "of the tabs has a very distinct"}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "layout."}, {"start": 241.0, "text": "So large titles in this case"}, {"start": 243.0, "text": "would compete with content."}, {"start": 247.0, "text": "Now let's take a closer look at"}, {"start": 249.0, "text": "ways that we can improve hierarchy through type."}, {"start": 252.0, "text": "Typographic hierarchy is the way"}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "to organize type in a way that"}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "will emphasize important content"}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "over less important content and"}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "it can help to group things"}, {"start": 262.0, "text": "together."}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "This can reduce cognitive load"}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "or the amount of mental effort"}, {"start": 267.0, "text": "it takes you to find something"}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "that you're looking for."}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "And there are a few basic"}, {"start": 272.0, "text": "methods for establishing"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "typographic hierarchy."}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "The position of the text can"}, {"start": 280.0, "text": "convey importance."}, {"start": 282.0, "text": "Since Label 1 is on top, we can"}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "infer that it's more important"}, {"start": 286.0, "text": "than Label 2, but that might not"}, {"start": 288.0, "text": "be obvious in all cases."}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "So another way is to decrease"}, {"start": 292.0, "text": "the size of the secondary line"}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "or you can vary the weight or"}, {"start": 297.0, "text": "you can use color so that the"}, {"start": 299.0, "text": "secondary line recedes more."}, {"start": 301.0, "text": "You may need to use more than"}, {"start": 303.0, "text": "one of these at a time so you"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "can make sure there's clear"}, {"start": 307.0, "text": "hierarchy between the two."}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "Here's a screen from photos in"}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "iOS 10."}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "The most important information"}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "here is your content, your"}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "photos."}, {"start": 319.0, "text": "The section headers use two text"}, {"start": 321.0, "text": "sizes to distinguish different"}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "information but all of it is a"}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "tad small and light."}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "So for iOS 11, we made section"}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "headers larger in general and"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "increased the text weight and"}, {"start": 334.0, "text": "used gray for supporting text."}, {"start": 337.0, "text": "And these changes made it easier"}, {"start": 339.0, "text": "to isolate important in content"}, {"start": 341.0, "text": "so that you can find a"}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "particular photo faster."}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "So let's look at more examples."}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "Here's Calendar in iOS 10."}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "We increased text weights for"}, {"start": 353.0, "text": "more emphasis and used color"}, {"start": 355.0, "text": "more intentionally to denote the"}, {"start": 357.0, "text": "current year, month, and date."}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "Here is Weather in iOS 10."}, {"start": 366.0, "text": "For iOS 11, we increased the"}, {"start": 368.0, "text": "text weights and made the text"}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "overall larger so that the"}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "content is easier to read."}, {"start": 376.0, "text": "So last, let's look at ways that"}, {"start": 378.0, "text": "we've tried to improve contrast."}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "To create more balance with the"}, {"start": 383.0, "text": "larger and more bold text styles"}, {"start": 385.0, "text": "throughout the UI, we needed to"}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "update other UI elements to give"}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "them greater contrast while"}, {"start": 391.0, "text": "keeping them both functional and"}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "minimal."}, {"start": 393.0, "text": "So one of the ways we did this"}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "was to fill in the button shapes"}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "and increase the size of the"}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "shape itself like we did with"}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "the search field."}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "And we updated the tab bars"}, {"start": 406.0, "text": "increasing the weight of the"}, {"start": 408.0, "text": "label from regular to medium."}, {"start": 412.0, "text": "And for the glyphs, we filled in"}, {"start": 414.0, "text": "the shapes and thickened the"}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "stroke weights."}, {"start": 418.0, "text": "And to make better use of space"}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "in landscape, we moved the label"}, {"start": 422.0, "text": "so that it's side by side with"}, {"start": 423.0, "text": "the glyph."}, {"start": 424.0, "text": "This tab bar is now shorter than"}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "before and now matches the"}, {"start": 428.0, "text": "landscape Nav bar and toolbar"}, {"start": 430.0, "text": "height. And a couple other things to"}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "note are that the glyphs are"}, {"start": 435.0, "text": "slightly smaller and the text is"}, {"start": 437.0, "text": "slightly larger than the"}, {"start": 439.0, "text": "portrait equivalents."}, {"start": 440.0, "text": "So you'll want to make sure you"}, {"start": 441.0, "text": "take that into account for your"}, {"start": 443.0, "text": "own apps."}, {"start": 446.0, "text": "On iPad, we can increase the"}, {"start": 447.0, "text": "text size even more while"}, {"start": 449.0, "text": "keeping the glyphs the same as"}, {"start": 451.0, "text": "portrait."}, {"start": 453.0, "text": "This is the Wallet app from iOS"}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "10. And typically we use material"}, {"start": 459.0, "text": "blurs to indicate when UI has"}, {"start": 461.0, "text": "come in on top of a page that is"}, {"start": 464.0, "text": "still underneath."}, {"start": 466.0, "text": "And we wanted to remove it in"}, {"start": 467.0, "text": "areas, like in this example,"}, {"start": 469.0, "text": "where it had no logical reason"}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "for being there and did not"}, {"start": 472.0, "text": "reinforce where you are in the"}, {"start": 474.0, "text": "digital space."}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "So that's a quick summary of the"}, {"start": 478.0, "text": "design updates we've made for"}, {"start": 480.0, "text": "iOS 11."}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "Keep these things in mind when"}, {"start": 483.0, "text": "making and updating your apps."}, {"start": 485.0, "text": "Use large-title navigation if"}, {"start": 488.0, "text": "areas of your app could use more"}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "emphasis and to help orient"}, {"start": 492.0, "text": "people."}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "But remember that it's not"}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "always necessary to use"}, {"start": 495.0, "text": "everywhere."}, {"start": 497.0, "text": "Consider whether your app could"}, {"start": 499.0, "text": "benefit from refining"}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "typographic hierarchy."}, {"start": 503.0, "text": "And lastly, remove superfluous"}, {"start": 505.0, "text": "UI elements and complexity to"}, {"start": 508.0, "text": "improve overall contrast in your"}, {"start": 511.0, "text": "app. We hope these updates will help"}, {"start": 513.0, "text": "you to create great products"}, {"start": 514.0, "text": "that are both beautiful and easy"}, {"start": 516.0, "text": "to use."}, {"start": 517.0, "text": "Thank you"}]}